nd":"content","content":[{"text":"Discussion","anchor":"discussion","level":2,"type":"heading"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Weights may be negative. Bellman–Ford from a virtual source joined to every vertex gives"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"each vertex "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"v"},{"type":"text","text":" a potential h(v), and Dijkstra’s algorithm runs from every vertex over the"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"reduced weights h(u) + w - h(v), which are nonnegative. Parallel edges count by their"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"cheapest. "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"findNegativeCycle(weight:)"},{"type":"text","text":" gives a negative cycle when this is "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"nil"},{"type":"text","text":". On sparse"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"graphs this is faster than "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"floydWarshallShortestPaths(weight:)"},{"type":"text","text":"."}],"type":"paragraph"},{"style":"note","name":"Complexity","content":[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"O(nm) for Bellman–Ford in the worst case (about one pass when no weight is"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"negative), then O(n · (n + m) log n); O(n²) space."}],"type":"paragraph"}],"type":"aside"},{"style":"note","name":"Precondition","content":[{"inlineContent":[{"text":"No weight is NaN; every sum fits in ","type":"text"},{"code":"W","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":", the reduced weights and the","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"reduced distances included. With floating point, distances are converted back from the","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"reduced ones and can differ from Floyd–Warshall’s by rounding.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"}],"type":"aside"}]}],"schemaVersion":{"patch":0,"major":0,"minor":3},"kind":"symbol","references":{"doc://ShortestPaths/documentation/ShortestPaths/DistanceMatrix":{"abstract":[{"type":"text",